    "created_at": "2017-07-28T02:10:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-28T02:34:19Z",
    "body": "I feel like every JavaScript API is like that, they are not meant to be convenient to use, but easy to implement. I admit that it is slowly moving  in the past years.\r\n\r\nThis being said, I'm ok with how it is right now. Mainly because every other API could be rewritten to make it more convenient to use in similar cases like this. But I've seen so many libraries that are just wrappers around the native stuff but make it friendlier, that I think that this would be the case for this.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
